WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:04.219
This is Part 8: the app, restock, and the truck card.

00:04.169 --> 00:05.720
The last part.

00:06.674 --> 00:09.749
Set up the app on the client's phone, not yours.

00:09.699 --> 00:12.742
Get the lights app from the App Store or Google Play.

00:12.742 --> 00:15.231
Make an account with the client's email.

00:15.231 --> 00:16.805
It's theirs for good.

00:16.805 --> 00:19.780
Check the box is on and the controller light is on.

00:19.780 --> 00:21.979
Tap plus to add a device.

00:21.979 --> 00:25.034
Pick Bluetooth, and tap the controller to pair.

00:25.034 --> 00:28.298
Then go to WiFi, and join the home network.

00:29.242 --> 00:35.071
In settings, set the IC type to Common RGBW, and the light count to the exact number put up.

00:35.021 --> 00:37.973
Try a pattern, and check every zone works.

00:37.973 --> 00:41.885
Set the sunset and sunrise timer, and show them how to change it.

00:41.885 --> 00:46.665
Then show the colour picker, patterns, holiday modes, the dimmer and the schedule.

00:47.610 --> 00:49.180
App problems.

00:49.130 --> 00:51.063
Can't find the controller?

00:51.063 --> 00:56.097
Stand within ten feet of the box, restart the box, and turn Bluetooth off and on.

00:56.097 --> 00:57.857
Lights ignore the app?

00:57.857 --> 01:02.614
The IC type is Common RGBW, and the light count matches exactly.

01:02.614 --> 01:04.535
WiFi won't connect?

01:04.535 --> 01:08.389
The router must use two point four gigahertz, not only five.

01:08.389 --> 01:10.692
Type the password again slowly.

01:10.692 --> 01:13.424
App says connected, but the lights are off?

01:13.424 --> 01:16.665
Check the box is on, and check for a tripped breaker.

01:16.665 --> 01:18.435
Zones not working?

01:18.435 --> 01:22.301
Set them again in settings, and check it's a PRO or PLUS controller.

01:23.258 --> 01:24.992
Handover tips.

01:24.942 --> 01:26.375
Let them do it.

01:26.375 --> 01:28.262
They need to feel sure.

01:28.262 --> 01:30.206
Show the sunset timer.

01:30.206 --> 01:32.058
They use it every day.

01:32.058 --> 01:34.049
Show holiday presets.

01:34.049 --> 01:35.796
That gets referrals.

01:35.796 --> 01:37.232
New phone?

01:37.232 --> 01:39.026
Just log in again.

01:39.026 --> 01:40.507
Box reset?

01:40.507 --> 01:42.220
They must pair again.

01:42.220 --> 01:46.178
Leave your number, and ask: would you mind leaving us a quick review?

01:46.178 --> 01:48.134
It really helps us grow.

01:49.090 --> 01:50.741
Restock Sunday.

01:50.691 --> 01:54.533
Every Sunday, or the last work day of the week, count your truck.

01:54.533 --> 01:59.510
Order anything under the minimum, and tell your supervisor about shortages by the end of Sunday.

01:59.510 --> 02:02.520
Sunday night orders come Monday or Tuesday.

02:02.520 --> 02:05.112
Running short on a job is not OK.

02:06.066 --> 02:07.786
Here are the minimums.

02:07.736 --> 02:09.496
Six hundred lights.

02:09.496 --> 02:11.810
One spare built power box.

02:11.810 --> 02:16.475
One spare six hundred watt supply, and two spare four fifty watt supplies.

02:16.475 --> 02:18.872
Six spare four amp breakers.

02:18.872 --> 02:24.438
Extensions: twenty one-footers, twenty two-footers, ten ten-footers, and five twenty-footers.

02:24.438 --> 02:31.648
Two rolls of sixteen-two FT-4 stranded wire, two rolls of corrugated conduit, and two tubes of dielectric grease.

02:32.618 --> 02:34.871
A hundred twenty metres of track.

02:34.821 --> 02:39.022
Ten L-connectors, ten straight connectors, and ten track end caps.

02:39.022 --> 02:43.860
Fifteen Y-connectors, ten T-injection connectors, and ten signal boosters.

02:43.860 --> 02:47.703
Twenty light end caps, and two hundred plus stainless screws.

02:47.703 --> 02:49.936
We use more injections now.

02:49.936 --> 02:55.561
With fifty lights per circuit, jobs need more T-connectors, feeder wire and breakers than before.

02:55.561 --> 02:57.541
These minimums are a start.

02:58.498 --> 03:00.936
Then the tools and PPE check.

03:00.886 --> 03:03.884
Drill charged, with bits and a spare battery.

03:03.884 --> 03:05.424
Snips sharp.

03:05.424 --> 03:06.870
Ladder checked.

03:06.870 --> 03:08.525
Glasses clear.

03:08.525 --> 03:10.134
Gloves OK.

03:10.134 --> 03:12.205
Hi-vis for each person.

03:12.205 --> 03:14.022
First aid kit full.

03:14.022 --> 03:17.599
And the clamp meter and multimeter work, with fresh batteries.

03:18.546 --> 03:20.590
Last, the truck card.

03:20.540 --> 03:22.728
Cut it out and keep it in the truck.

03:22.728 --> 03:26.420
The numbers: fifty lights per circuit, max fifty-six.

03:26.420 --> 03:30.656
Three point two amps max, and seventy-seven watts max per circuit.

03:30.656 --> 03:32.751
Five circuits per box.

03:32.751 --> 03:36.293
A six hundred watt box is four eighty watts and twenty amps.

03:36.293 --> 03:39.765
A four fifty is three sixty watts and fifteen amps.

03:39.765 --> 03:42.878
Twenty-two point eight volts minimum at the last light.

03:42.878 --> 03:46.513
And feeder is sixteen-two FT-4, thirty feet.

03:47.474 --> 03:50.641
The math: lights are feet times one point five.

03:50.591 --> 03:53.797
Circuits are lights divided by fifty, rounded up.

03:53.797 --> 03:57.073
Boxes are circuits divided by five, rounded up.

03:57.073 --> 04:01.887
Watts are lights times one point three seven, and amps are watts divided by twenty-four.

04:01.887 --> 04:05.834
Check fifty-six or less, and three point two amps or less.

04:05.834 --> 04:08.994
And every time: power off before you plug in.

04:08.994 --> 04:11.725
Test on Pure White, never a colour.

04:11.725 --> 04:14.214
Cut the positive at every injection.

04:14.214 --> 04:16.262
Never cut the data wire.

04:16.262 --> 04:18.103
Grease every connector.

04:18.103 --> 04:19.955
Never a bigger breaker.

04:19.955 --> 04:23.068
And tests A, B and C before you leave.

04:24.034 --> 04:25.268
Recap.

04:25.218 --> 04:28.424
The app goes on the client's phone, with their email.

04:28.424 --> 04:32.440
IC type Common RGBW, and the exact light count.

04:32.440 --> 04:35.241
Show the sunset timer, and let them do it.

04:35.241 --> 04:38.864
Count the truck every Sunday, and order anything under the minimum.

04:38.864 --> 04:41.098
And keep the truck card in the truck.

04:42.066 --> 04:44.585
That's Part 8, and the whole course.

04:44.535 --> 04:47.463
Now take the Part 8 quiz in your training portal.
